1
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:00,520
Do you remember

2
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:02,359
how First Wife died?

3
00:01:02,799 --> 00:01:04,799
Should I tell them?

4
00:01:05,280 --> 00:01:06,000
First Wife...

5
00:01:06,760 --> 00:01:08,319
Her soul was stolen by the Flower Demon.

6
00:01:14,719 --> 00:01:15,319
First Wife!

7
00:01:15,640 --> 00:01:16,680
First Wife has returned!

8
00:01:16,760 --> 00:01:17,959
Oh, First Wife!

9
00:01:21,319 --> 00:01:21,719
Chunmei,

10
00:01:22,599 --> 00:01:23,519
First Wife...

11
00:01:24,040 --> 00:01:24,640
What's her background?

12
00:01:26,439 --> 00:01:27,640
First Wife's family

13
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:29,599
is the biggest tea merchant in Lijia Town.

14
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:34,239
First Wife loved flowers.

15
00:01:35,120 --> 00:01:36,239
After marrying into the Li Manor,

16
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:38,599
she planted flowers all over the garden.

17
00:01:40,120 --> 00:01:41,280
Besides planting flowers,

18
00:01:41,840 --> 00:01:42,719
she also loved drinking tea.

19
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:46,599
Whenever the tea shop got new tea,

20
00:01:47,319 --> 00:01:49,480
First Wife would personally brew it

21
00:01:49,519 --> 00:01:50,439
for Master Li to try.

22
00:01:51,959 --> 00:01:53,719
The couple had a harmonious relationship,

23
00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:55,920
and lived a very peaceful life.

24
00:02:02,439 --> 00:02:03,359
Until that day...

25
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:05,239
the Flower Demon came.

26
00:02:13,039 --> 00:02:14,080
When the Flower Demon arrived,

27
00:02:14,919 --> 00:02:15,879
a gust of wind blew.

28
00:02:17,039 --> 00:02:19,000
The Flower Demon drained their essence,

29
00:02:19,319 --> 00:02:20,280
making them wither instantly.

30
00:02:29,919 --> 00:02:32,360
The Flower Demon also targeted First Wife.

31
00:02:33,960 --> 00:02:34,879
On that very day,

32
00:02:35,840 --> 00:02:37,240
First Wife, just like always,

33
00:02:37,479 --> 00:02:38,400
was brewing tea for the master.

34
00:02:39,879 --> 00:02:40,800
But the Flower Demon

35
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:42,800
didn't spare her.

36
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:54,759
Madam!

37
00:02:56,759 --> 00:02:57,400
Somebody, help!

38
00:02:58,479 --> 00:02:59,240
Somebody come quick!

39
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:04,639
First Wife is dead!

40
00:03:04,759 --> 00:03:05,960
Why didn't you call the police?

41
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:07,560
Of course we called the police.

42
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:09,639
Master Li even asked Chief Mu to investigate.

43
00:03:09,879 --> 00:03:10,439
But...

44
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:12,800
Chief Mu.

45
00:03:13,039 --> 00:03:14,199
You're finally here.

46
00:03:19,319 --> 00:03:20,080
Chief Mu.

47
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,800
First Wife was perfectly fine.

48
00:03:23,479 --> 00:03:24,879
How did she suddenly die?

49
00:03:26,719 --> 00:03:28,800
She had no external injuries.

50
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:32,439
And we found no poison in the manor.

51
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:36,039
We really can't determine the cause of death.

52
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:39,960
Do you think First Wife...

53
00:03:40,159 --> 00:03:41,520
...had some hidden illness...

54
00:03:42,080 --> 00:03:43,360
...and died from a sudden attack?

55
00:03:44,280 --> 00:03:45,639
First Wife was in great health.

56
00:03:45,879 --> 00:03:46,879
What hidden illness could she have?

57
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:49,120
It was the Flower Demon that killed her.

58
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:51,840
The so-called Flower Demon...

59
00:03:52,039 --> 00:03:53,800
...is often found in ancient monster tales.

60
00:03:54,719 --> 00:03:57,080
Flowers turning into spirits to harm mortals.

61
00:03:57,280 --> 00:03:58,080
Don't talk nonsense.

62
00:03:58,840 --> 00:03:59,879
We're investigating a case right now.

63
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:01,520
Not writing a storybook.

64
00:04:01,919 --> 00:04:02,360
Chunmei.

65
00:04:03,719 --> 00:04:04,639
Did First Wife...

66
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:07,199
...wear a white qipao?

67
00:04:08,280 --> 00:04:09,039
Yes, how did...

68
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:10,400
How did you know?

69
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:13,080
We all saw it.

70
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:14,800
First Wife really became a ghost.

71
00:04:20,240 --> 00:04:21,639
Look at how timid you are.

72
00:04:21,639 --> 00:04:23,079
There's no such thing as ghosts or demons.

73
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:25,279
We must believe in science.

74
00:04:25,279 --> 00:04:27,040
Stop spreading feudal superstitions.

75
00:04:27,079 --> 00:04:27,680
She-devil!

76
00:04:30,959 --> 00:04:31,360
Chunmei,

77
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:34,160
Keep preparing the wedding clothes.

78
00:04:34,519 --> 00:04:35,199
We're going for a walk.

79
00:04:38,319 --> 00:04:40,800
What do we do? They're going to investigate.

80
00:04:41,199 --> 00:04:41,720
Master.

81
00:04:42,439 --> 00:04:43,600
First Wife's grave is right there.

82
00:04:44,360 --> 00:04:45,279
Are we really going to open the coffin?

83
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:47,040
What if it attracts the Flower Demon?

84
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:48,879
Flower Demon.

85
00:04:49,399 --> 00:04:50,600
I'd like to see what she looks like.

86
00:04:56,079 --> 00:04:56,759
What did you find?

87
00:04:57,680 --> 00:04:58,560
First Wife's grave...

88
00:04:59,879 --> 00:05:01,839
...why is it the exact same shape as the Li Manor?

89
00:05:02,959 --> 00:05:03,800
Both are Haunted Houses.

90
00:05:04,199 --> 00:05:05,120
A Haunted House?

91
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:08,240
How can you tell it's a Haunted House?

92
00:05:08,519 --> 00:05:10,040
It's mentioned in The Classic of Lu Ban.

93
00:05:10,759 --> 00:05:13,040
If built wide in front, narrow in back,

94
00:05:13,439 --> 00:05:14,560
it will be restless all year round.

95
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:15,959
Energy leaks, turning it ominous.

96
00:05:16,639 --> 00:05:18,519
The Li Manor is built exactly like that.

97
00:05:19,079 --> 00:05:19,759
But I never expected...

98
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:22,079
First Wife's grave to be the same shape.

99
00:05:23,199 --> 00:05:24,079
That's strange.

100
00:05:24,959 --> 00:05:27,480
Why make both the manor and the grave

101
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:29,160
into Haunted Houses?

102
00:05:31,079 --> 00:05:32,120
What nonsense.

103
00:05:32,839 --> 00:05:34,480
Who cares if it's a manor or a grave?

104
00:05:34,759 --> 00:05:36,000
Aren't they just built of wood and lime?

105
00:05:36,439 --> 00:05:37,360
What's so haunted about them?

106
00:05:37,720 --> 00:05:38,519
In my opinion,

107
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:39,800
the only things that harm people...

108
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:40,560
...are people.

109
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:55,959
First Wife.

110
00:05:56,680 --> 00:05:57,240
Sorry for the intrusion.

111
00:05:57,839 --> 00:05:58,480
Please forgive us.

112
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:16,000
First Wife didn't die of illness.

113
00:06:16,279 --> 00:06:17,040
She died of poisoning.

114
00:06:17,519 --> 00:06:18,160
Poisoning?

115
00:06:18,560 --> 00:06:18,959
Yes.

116
00:06:22,199 --> 00:06:23,639
There are no signs of poison on the body.

117
00:06:24,079 --> 00:06:25,319
So my dad couldn't determine the cause.

118
00:06:27,959 --> 00:06:28,519
Strange.

119
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:31,959
In First Wife's blood,

120
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:34,600
why is there a scent of plants?

121
00:06:35,120 --> 00:06:36,000
You have a dog's nose.

122
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:37,160
It's that sensitive?

123
00:06:39,439 --> 00:06:41,160
When I was a kid, I hated studying.

124
00:06:41,720 --> 00:06:42,199
So my dad

125
00:06:42,399 --> 00:06:43,759
would hide all the tasty food.

126
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:46,279
If I didn't study, he wouldn't let me eat.

127
00:06:46,959 --> 00:06:48,480
But no matter where he hid it,

128
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:49,360
I could always find it.

129
00:06:50,199 --> 00:06:51,879
Over time, with all that sniffing,

130
00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:53,480
my sense of smell just got sharper.

131
00:06:54,279 --> 00:06:55,480
So your nose

132
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:56,600
can only smell food.

133
00:06:57,879 --> 00:06:58,560
Not exactly.

134
00:06:59,079 --> 00:07:01,360
My dad forced me to study Bencao Gangmu.

135
00:07:01,680 --> 00:07:03,959
He made me smell every herb in the world.

136
00:07:04,439 --> 00:07:05,800
Back then, going into the mountains...

137
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:09,519
What's wrong?

138
00:07:11,199 --> 00:07:11,839
I remember now.

139
00:07:12,920 --> 00:07:13,800
I've smelled this scent before.

140
00:07:14,519 --> 00:07:15,199
It was at the Li Manor.

141
00:07:15,360 --> 00:07:16,399
When we passed by the garden.

142
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:18,759
Okay. Pack this up.

143
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:19,600
Let's go to the garden.

144
00:07:19,879 --> 00:07:20,279
Okay.

145
00:07:20,279 --> 00:07:20,879
I'm not going.

146
00:07:21,639 --> 00:07:23,079
That garden must have a Flower Demon.

147
00:07:23,480 --> 00:07:25,480
First Wife was killed by the Flower Demon.

148
00:07:26,439 --> 00:07:26,879
Fine.

149
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:28,439
Then in a bit,

150
00:07:28,839 --> 00:07:29,600
you can stay right here

151
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:31,120
and tell stories to First Wife.

152
00:07:32,639 --> 00:07:33,279
She-devil!

153
00:07:33,399 --> 00:07:33,920
Alright, I...

154
00:07:34,439 --> 00:07:34,920
Stop messing around.

155
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:36,560
Solving the case is what matters.

156
00:07:37,199 --> 00:07:37,759
Hurry up.

157
00:07:38,120 --> 00:07:38,480
Quick.

158
00:07:39,360 --> 00:07:39,800
Hold this.

159
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:41,360
Come on.

160
00:07:48,120 --> 00:07:49,279
This is First Wife's garden.

161
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:51,360
Before First Wife died,

162
00:07:51,879 --> 00:07:52,759
something strange happened in the garden.

163
00:07:53,720 --> 00:07:54,959
The flowers she painstakingly grew

164
00:07:55,519 --> 00:07:56,439
all died overnight.

165
00:07:57,600 --> 00:07:58,240
Tell me,

166
00:07:58,959 --> 00:08:00,879
do these flowers and First Wife's death

167
00:08:01,199 --> 00:08:01,920
have anything to do with each other?

168
00:08:05,240 --> 00:08:06,079
Oleander.

169
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:08,959
The scent on First Wife's remains

170
00:08:09,600 --> 00:08:10,279
is exactly the same.

171
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:11,759
Oleander.

172
00:08:13,079 --> 00:08:14,079
This flower is highly toxic.

173
00:08:14,720 --> 00:08:15,439
Once poisoned,

174
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:16,720
it causes convulsions,

175
00:08:17,079 --> 00:08:17,959
heart failure,

176
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:19,120
and even coughing up blood.

177
00:08:20,199 --> 00:08:20,759
It seems

178
00:08:21,480 --> 00:08:23,079
First Wife was poisoned by Oleander.

179
00:08:26,399 --> 00:08:26,839
What is it?

180
00:08:29,160 --> 00:08:30,959
There's a lot of Caustic Soda in the soil.

181
00:08:33,120 --> 00:08:34,559
What withered the flowers in the garden

182
00:08:34,840 --> 00:08:35,600
wasn't some Flower Demon.

183
00:08:37,840 --> 00:08:39,279
It was the Caustic Soda in this soil.

184
00:08:39,919 --> 00:08:41,039
Caustic Soda is highly corrosive.

185
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:42,399
So,

186
00:08:43,039 --> 00:08:44,279
that's what caused the plants to die.

187
00:08:45,200 --> 00:08:46,600
I'm a little confused.

188
00:08:47,279 --> 00:08:48,120
Why would the killer

189
00:08:48,279 --> 00:08:50,320
want to destroy all these plants?

190
00:08:50,879 --> 00:08:51,720
To destroy evidence.

191
00:08:53,360 --> 00:08:55,559
By destroying the garden's plants,

192
00:08:56,639 --> 00:08:58,200
the police couldn't trace the poison.

193
00:08:59,279 --> 00:09:00,399
But I still don't think it makes sense.

194
00:09:01,320 --> 00:09:03,600
First Wife knew everything about flowers.

195
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:06,399
Why would she ingest Oleander poison?

196
00:09:08,840 --> 00:09:10,360
First Wife loved drinking tea.

197
00:09:11,320 --> 00:09:13,519
The tea is stored in the warehouse.

198
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:15,480
Let's go check the warehouse.

199
00:09:15,639 --> 00:09:16,360
Maybe we'll find some clues.

200
00:09:16,799 --> 00:09:17,159
Let's go.

201
00:09:46,840 --> 00:09:48,159
Born into a family of tea merchants,

202
00:09:49,159 --> 00:09:50,759
knowing tea inside out since childhood.

203
00:09:54,799 --> 00:09:55,679
Pu'er is mellow,

204
00:09:56,799 --> 00:09:57,720
Longjing is crisp.

205
00:09:58,720 --> 00:10:00,320
What tea did you really drink that day?

206
00:10:24,279 --> 00:10:25,480
March 7th, four months ago.

207
00:10:26,120 --> 00:10:27,519
First Wife died right after drinking tea.

208
00:10:29,440 --> 00:10:30,200
What tea?

209
00:10:32,080 --> 00:10:32,840
On March 6th,

210
00:10:33,159 --> 00:10:34,679
Dai's Tea Shop sent five packs of new tea.

211
00:10:35,120 --> 00:10:35,600
It was called

212
00:10:36,320 --> 00:10:37,240
Desert Rose Tea.

213
00:10:40,360 --> 00:10:42,440
Desert Rose Tea. Desert Rose Tea.

214
00:10:42,879 --> 00:10:44,120
It's my first time hearing of this tea.

215
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:54,840
This Desert Rose,

216
00:10:55,200 --> 00:10:57,080
in both appearance and smell,

217
00:10:57,600 --> 00:10:58,960
is very similar to Oleander.

218
00:11:01,159 --> 00:11:01,960
It seems the killer

219
00:11:02,799 --> 00:11:04,399
used the Oleander from the garden

220
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:05,720
to replace the Desert Rose.

221
00:11:06,440 --> 00:11:07,279
So First Wife

222
00:11:07,440 --> 00:11:09,039
drank the highly toxic Oleander

223
00:11:09,840 --> 00:11:10,720
and was poisoned to death.

224
00:11:11,320 --> 00:11:13,639
Does this killer really hate rich people?

225
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:14,480
Look,

226
00:11:14,879 --> 00:11:16,080
Mengzhu was a wealthy lady,

227
00:11:16,360 --> 00:11:18,000
and First Wife was also rich.

228
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:22,120
Chunmei said on the day First Wife died,

229
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:24,399
Master Li had mouth sores

230
00:11:24,720 --> 00:11:25,440
and couldn't drink hot tea.

231
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:27,759
So he didn't drink

232
00:11:27,919 --> 00:11:29,600
the Desert Rose Tea First Wife prepared.

233
00:11:31,679 --> 00:11:32,840
My deduction was right.

234
00:11:33,840 --> 00:11:34,799
The killer's target

235
00:11:35,639 --> 00:11:36,360
was Master Li.

236
00:11:36,840 --> 00:11:37,960
But they accidentally killed First Wife.

237
00:11:38,559 --> 00:11:40,159
So Mengzhu was also killed by mistake?

238
00:11:40,279 --> 00:11:40,759
Exactly.

239
00:11:54,919 --> 00:11:55,960
My three wives,

240
00:11:57,279 --> 00:11:57,879
Mengzhu,

241
00:12:00,159 --> 00:12:02,320
I didn't take good care of you.

242
00:12:03,840 --> 00:12:05,720
I'm truly sorry.

243
00:12:07,679 --> 00:12:08,879
May your spirits in heaven

244
00:12:10,080 --> 00:12:11,480
please protect me

245
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:13,240
and keep me safe.

246
00:12:28,519 --> 00:12:29,360
Chief Mu.

247
00:12:32,279 --> 00:12:32,799
That's not right.

248
00:12:33,559 --> 00:12:34,279
Madam.

249
00:12:37,480 --> 00:12:38,960
We're getting married tomorrow morning.

250
00:12:39,960 --> 00:12:40,879
My father already told me.

251
00:12:41,679 --> 00:12:42,159
But,

252
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:44,559
he asked me, before I marry you,

253
00:12:44,799 --> 00:12:46,240
to look into the Li family murders first.

254
00:12:46,840 --> 00:12:47,440
Sure.

255
00:12:48,200 --> 00:12:50,360
The whole Li manor is your home now.

256
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:51,720
Investigate as you please.

257
00:12:53,519 --> 00:12:54,000
Okay.

258
00:12:55,440 --> 00:12:56,200
Then you must also know

259
00:12:57,200 --> 00:12:58,559
that current evidence shows

260
00:12:59,559 --> 00:13:00,799
you are the killer's target.

261
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:04,720
Then you'd better protect me well.

262
00:13:05,679 --> 00:13:06,720
From now on,

263
00:13:06,960 --> 00:13:08,840
you need to stay by my side at all times.

264
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,720
Then tell me the truth first.

265
00:13:11,759 --> 00:13:12,879
Do you have any enemies at all?

266
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:14,759
You wrong me, Madam!

267
00:13:16,440 --> 00:13:18,240
Who could I have a grudge against?

268
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:21,120
Everyone calls me Benefactor Li.

269
00:13:21,759 --> 00:13:22,879
Do you know why?

270
00:13:23,480 --> 00:13:24,720
In the past, Lijia Town

271
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:26,840
was dirt poor.

272
00:13:27,679 --> 00:13:29,320
Ever since I came to Lijia Town,

273
00:13:30,039 --> 00:13:32,399
I paid to build bridges and pave roads.

274
00:13:32,960 --> 00:13:34,519
I opened a gold shop for business

275
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:36,039
and boosted the economy.

276
00:13:36,639 --> 00:13:37,200
So,

277
00:13:37,679 --> 00:13:39,240
everyone calls me Benefactor Li.

278
00:13:40,279 --> 00:13:42,840
So everyone in town could live well,

279
00:13:43,480 --> 00:13:45,120
I donated both money and goods.

280
00:13:45,799 --> 00:13:47,799
Who could I have a grudge against?

281
00:13:48,399 --> 00:13:49,480
It's the Flowing Cloud Pattern again.

282
00:13:50,799 --> 00:13:51,840
Why does the Li family have so many

283
00:13:51,919 --> 00:13:52,919
items from the Yuncang Kingdom?

284
00:13:53,799 --> 00:13:54,879
You really don't have any enemies?

285
00:13:55,240 --> 00:13:56,440
It's the absolute truth!

286
00:13:57,120 --> 00:13:59,519
I even paid to build your police station.

287
00:14:00,080 --> 00:14:01,480
Right now, half of Lijia Town

288
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:03,279
was built using my funds.

289
00:14:03,840 --> 00:14:05,200
Who would I have a grudge against?

290
00:14:06,240 --> 00:14:07,279
That's strange then.

291
00:14:07,919 --> 00:14:09,519
We must find the motive first

292
00:14:10,480 --> 00:14:11,600
to track down the killer.

293
00:14:12,399 --> 00:14:13,759
The people of Lijia Town

294
00:14:13,919 --> 00:14:15,279
have all benefited from you.

295
00:14:16,159 --> 00:14:17,200
They have no reason to kill you.

296
00:14:29,039 --> 00:14:29,440
Who's there?
